From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reelee81 <reelee81@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:12:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] pdf: Skip the rest of a number that is too long.

lex_number() reads a number into the lexer buffer and stops when the
buffer is full: the remaining digits stay in the stream and are read as
the next token. Inside a dictionary that token is a number where a key
is expected, so the whole object fails to parse ("invalid key in dict");
the pdf.js test filled-background.pdf has a /Pi entry of 100 001
characters in the resources of its pages. Like an over-long name, which
lex_name() already truncates, the rest of such a number is now read and
dropped with a warning, and the number keeps the value of its first
characters (255 in content streams, 65 535 in objects).

Modified for ReePDF on 2026-11-15.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 source/pdf/pdf-lex.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/source/pdf/pdf-lex.c b/source/pdf/pdf-lex.c
index aaee6af..d5b7851 100644
--- a/source/pdf/pdf-lex.c
+++ b/source/pdf/pdf-lex.c
@@ -242,6 +242,33 @@ lex_number(fz_context *ctx, fz_stream *f, pdf_lexbuf *buf, int c)
 		c = lex_byte(ctx, f);
 	}
 
+	/* skip the rest of numbers that are too long */
+	fz_warn(ctx, "number is too long");
+	while (1)
+	{
+		switch (c)
+		{
+		case IS_WHITE:
+		case IS_DELIM:
+			fz_unread_byte(ctx, f);
+			goto end;
+		case EOF:
+			goto end;
+		case '.':
+			if (isreal)
+				isbad = 1;
+			isreal = s;
+			break;
+		case '-':
+		case RANGE_0_9:
+			break;
+		default:
+			isbad = 1;
+			break;
+		}
+		c = lex_byte(ctx, f);
+	}
+
 end:
 	*s = '\0';
 	if (isbad)
